    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"resistance\" part, but it feels like a loop. if the universe is indifferent, then the \"meaning\" we create is also just a temporary hallucination, right? it feels like we're just performing for an empty room. at some point, isn't it more intellectually honest to admit that there's no reason to keep performing? it feels exhausting to keep pretending there's a point when the logic just doesn't hold up.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
